{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1494476-foundations-and-pillars-that-didn-t-appear","id":1494476,"title":"Foundations and Pillars that didn't appear","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-06T16:35:37-07:00","id":1494476,"title":"Foundations and Pillars that didn't appear","content":"Hi folks. So we have Dark Ages: Mage Pillars and Foundations for almost all of the groups that'd become the traditions,I'm wondering what would the the Foundation/Pillars of the groups that would become the Sahajya/Cult of Ecstasy and the Kahu/Kopa Loei <br /> Do you have ideas on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T20:43:41-07:00","id":1494492,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong; but the Kopa Loei were never a Tradition. Right? The Akashayana, on the other hand\u2026<br /> <br /> Start with some research into where the groups originated. The ancestors of the Sahajiya were scattered during the Dark Ages; if they are to have Fellowships in that age, they need to be like the Old Faith or the Spirit-Talkers. In Europe, anyway. Likewise, the Akashayana had no substantial presence in Europe. <br /> <br /> In Asia, on the other hand, I could see putting together no less than four Fellowships: the Akashayana and their ancient enemies, the Chakravanti; the Sahajiya; and the Wu Lung.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T07:15:03-07:00","id":1494522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1494476-foundations-and-pillars-that-didn-t-appear?p=1494492#post1494492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong; but the Kopa Loei were never a Tradition. Right? The Akashayana, on the other hand\u2026<br /> <br /> Start with some research into where the groups originated. The ancestors of the Sahajiya were scattered during the Dark Ages; if they are to have Fellowships in that age, they need to be like the Old Faith or the Spirit-Talkers. In Europe, anyway. Likewise, the Akashayana had no substantial presence in Europe. <br /> <br /> In Asia, on the other hand, I could see putting together no less than four Fellowships: the Akashayana and their ancient enemies, the Chakravanti; the Sahajiya; and the Wu Lung.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Any ideas for pillars and foundations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T07:40:56-07:00","id":1494523,"title":"","content":"For the Akashayana, I'd look to Do as inspiration for the Foundation, and the Eight Limbs of Expertise (M20 p.428) for ideas concerning the Pillars. In the latter case, see if you can come up with four pairs, like Dharmamuki/Shastamarga as one pairing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T07:45:55-07:00","id":1494524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1494476-foundations-and-pillars-that-didn-t-appear?p=1494523#post1494523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Akashayana, I'd look to Do as inspiration for the Foundation, and the Eight Limbs of Expertise (M20 p.428) for ideas concerning the Pillars. In the latter case, see if you can come up with four pairs, like Dharmamuki/Shastamarga as one pairing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the researchcopter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T09:40:02-07:00","id":1494789,"title":"","content":"Search this forum. I know that there have been writeups for the Akashayana, the Chakravanti and others in various threads over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T09:51:16-07:00","id":1494792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1494476-foundations-and-pillars-that-didn-t-appear?p=1494789#post1494789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Search this forum. I know that there have been writeups for the Akashayana, the Chakravanti and others in various threads over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Cadmiun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T16:56:19-07:00","id":1495205,"title":"","content":"I've got a blast from the past... Malcolm Shephard actually wrote up the Chakravanti and the Akashics for DA: Mage<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chakravanti? Sure, but remember that they're one of many groups during the DA period. The Euthanatos Tradition has not been created yet. In Europe in the period covered by the line, there are: # The Knights of St. Gregory of Nyssa (a recognized knightly order that serves as a cover for the worshippers off Radamanthys)<br /> <br /> # The Ixoi (they have not yet split into the Golden Chalice and Ksrafai)<br /> # The Pomegranate Deme and the The Aided (probably both Old Faith right now, but with a slightly different Foundation. The Aided are actually outcast from the main Old Faith, because they violate the pagan virtues. The Pomegranate Deme are protected by the Gregorian Knights).<br /> # The Valdaermen (part of the Fellowship is incorporated into the Euthanatos Tradition as the Gallowsmen)<br /> # The Pollottino family (a small family of &quot;white necromancers who use Etruscan rituals,&quot; and enemies of the Giovanni family)<br /> <br /> The Chakravanti comprise the:<br /> # Lahksmists (followers of the divine principle of fortune)<br /> # Sapindya Sadananda (the Fellowship's warriors and assassins -- also known as the Consanguinity of Eternal Joy. Currently ruled by the necromancer Helekar).<br /> # Natatapas (your &quot;average&quot; Tantrist Chakravanti, somewhat matrirachal in outlook).<br /> <br /> We can give them all the same Foundation and Pillars, though.<br /> <br /> Foundation: Duty (Dharma)<br /> The Chakravanti believe that mystical power and enlightenment come through adherence to one's karmically ordained duty. Average people perform the duties mandated by their caste; Chakravanti have the onerous duty of correcting people and groups when they fall astray of that duty through corruption or by clinging to a distraction. When performed correctly, the Chakravat Duty is equated to the positions of the gods and beyond that, the uncreated power that exists beyond the gods. Thus, proper performance of Duty gives godlike attributes.<br /> <br /> Pillars: Lokha<br /> <br /> Lokha (worlds) are layers of existence that are both states of being and actual places that the soul (Atman) incarnates. There are six Lokha in total:<br /> # The demonic Lohka (Naraka)<br /> # The ghostly Lokha (Preta)<br /> # The animal Lokha (Triyagoni)<br /> # The human Lokha (Manu)<br /> # The Lokha of the warring demigods (Asura)<br /> # The divine Lokha (Deva)<br /> <br /> The human Lokha is already within the mage. It is practiced through adherence to Dharma. The Asura Lokha is a false path practiced by other supernatural beings. So the Pillars are:<br /> # Naraka: Punishment and destruction, cursing.<br /> # Preta: Necromancy<br /> # Triyagoni: Healing the body and controlling base desires.<br /> # Deva: Manipulating the fundamental forces of the universe (like Quintessence), taking in divine characteristics, blessings. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Foundation:<br /> In this period, we call the Foundation the Vajra (&quot;diamond&quot; or &quot;thunderbolt&quot;),<br /> represented the dynamic potential of anlightenment. Some Tibetan Akashics will<br /> call it Dralaphurba (&quot;windhorse-thunder&quot;) which will later be known as<br /> Draladhrama, the modern syncretic term. Their aura penalizes rolls which require<br /> expressing intimacy.<br /> <br /> Akashics have an aura of emptiness, like they are a vast, empty space that<br /> consumes the unprepared.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: Normal and supernatural Social rolls have a +1 difficulty due to the<br /> Akashic's subtle nature.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: Attempts to alter the Akashic's mind with supernatural powers (Doiminate,<br /> Obligation, Crona, etc.) face a +1 difficulty penalty since the Akashic's mind<br /> becomes consumed with esoteric symbols wrapped around an empty space.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: The Akashic's body now obeys formless, esoteric patterns that are almost<br /> unpredictable. Opponents now face a +1 difficulty penalty to strike with physical<br /> attacks, unless they directly target the character's pattern.<br /> Pillars:<br /> <br /> The four pillars are called &quot;kaya&quot; (&quot;bodies&quot;). These correspond to the different<br /> paths to enlightenment and the different elemental symbols of reality.<br /> <br /> The Nirmanakaya is the Scarlet Phoenix-Body. This corresponds to the the physical<br /> body, as well as practices based on everyday observance and society at large.<br /> <br /> Many physical applications of Do sping from this Pillar. This Pillar is rigid and<br /> emphasizes custom.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: Sense the flow of propriety in a being or place; whether a person is<br /> healthy, whether Quintessence flows naturally through a place (instaed of being<br /> twisted or snagged) and whether a person is speaking honestly.<br /> <br /> Rank 2: Can use proper medicine and exercise to heal oneself of bashing or lethal<br /> damage, can smooth chi flow along its proper course (but not determine what that<br /> course is; he can return strength to a Dragon Nest, but not add extra strength to<br /> it) and can detect supernatural compulsion in others and ward it off in himself.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: Learns proper rigid forms to increase physical prowess, medicine to heal<br /> bashing and lethal in others and aggravated in himself. The Akashic can also ward<br /> off supernatural compulsion in a person or area.<br /> <br /> Rank 4: The Akashic can force people or spirits to obey any vow they willingly<br /> make. He can heal aggravated wounds in others by using traditional medicine and<br /> sustain his body with discipline so strong that it can ward off fire and shatter<br /> swords and spears.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: The Akashic is a disciplined master of external rigid power and internal<br /> sensitivity to the structure of the Tapestry. He can enter Heaven (the Astral<br /> Umbra) at will and cannot be cut off from the universe, since he can use rites<br /> and exercises to take chi from anywhere.<br /> <br /> The Sambhokaya is the Pearl Tiger-Body. It is the Pillar of communication and of<br /> opening oneself to invisible realms. Akashic who deal with the gods make use of<br /> this kaya.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: The Akashic can peer into the Umbra and can improve his ability to<br /> communicate (-1 difficulty/success), but not use telepathy or languages that he<br /> does not know. He can see if active spirits are possessing people or places.<br /> <br /> Rank 2: The Akashic can sense emotions and can engage in voluntarily telepathic<br /> speech with others, including spirits on the other side of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: The Akashic can telepathically communicate with anyone and can even<br /> overcome resistance. He can enter dreams and send terrible visions (inflicting<br /> bashing damage) to people or spirits. He can even reach into the Umbra while<br /> staying in the normal world.<br /> <br /> Rank 4: Communication with even slumbering spirits is possible, and the Akashic<br /> can even speak to past incarnations of entities through the Akashic Record. The<br /> mage can makes spirits visible and tangible to others, as well. All this<br /> information allows him to avoid surprise and improve alertness with bonuses to<br /> defensive dice pools.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: Akashics can communicate with something to the extent that they become<br /> that thing, animating a statue, rock, person or spirit, whether they like it or<br /> not. The character can also speak directly to patterns allowing him to animate or<br /> destroy them (aggravated, resisted by Willpower).<br /> <br /> The Dharmakaya is also called the Dragon-Body and represents the dissolution of<br /> preconceived ideas. Akashic tap this with internal martial arts, quiet meditation<br /> and austerity. The student leaves behind illusions to see things as they are,<br /> leading to simple but powerful magic.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: The Akashic can see through illusions, including mundane disguises and<br /> magical deceptions, and even fients and distractions in combat (grants an<br /> initiative bonus)<br /> <br /> Rank 2: You would say that the Akashic could &quot;divide&quot; his mind, but really, the mind expands to encompass many things. A spell allows the character to fully concentrate on multiple nonmagical actions (1 for each arm in addition to one spell, usually). The Akashic can also let his sense of self dissolve, becoming silent or invisible.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: The Akashic abandons egotism in movement and sees that time is arbitrary (allowing multiple actions) and sees the natural flaws in structure (allowing extra damage). He can also honestly judge the abilities of others (determining their traits with a spell, so long as the character could see them in action).<br /> <br /> Rank 4: The character's sense of place is an illusion; he can teleport from place<br /> to place and affect things from a distance.<br /> <br /> rank 5: The mage can now be many places at once and can provide minds for each<br /> node of experience. He realizes all living chi belongs to a single, cosmic flow<br /> and can siphon it to and from other creatures.<br /> <br /> Swabhavakaya, the Windhorse-Body is the path of black magic and quick, brutal<br /> esoteric training. It tranforms the Akashic into a living mystical symbol, able<br /> to change other symbols and thus, the creatures attached to them. It includes<br /> dangerous arts like karma manipulation.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: By studying omens and meditative visions, the character can sense the odds of a future event and recognize mighty or infamous destinies.<br /> Blah, blah, blah. You guys do the rest. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T17:04:19-07:00","id":1495206,"title":"","content":"A big thank you to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T18:54:02-07:00","id":1495210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1494476-foundations-and-pillars-that-didn-t-appear?p=1495205#post1495205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Chakravanti?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this the same system used for the Nagaraja ancestor mages used as blood familiars in guide to the talmahera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T23:02:10-07:00","id":1495222,"title":"","content":"Yes; yes, it is. <br /> <br /> In terms of the original Traditions, we have Foundation and Pillars for: <br /> \u2022 Ahl-i-Batin<br /> \u2022 Idran (Euthanatos)<br /> \u2022 Messianic Voices (Celestial Chorus)<br /> \u2022 Old Faith (Verbena)<br /> \u2022 Order of Hermes<br /> \u2022 Spirit Talkers (Dreamspeakers)<br /> \u2026and with Malcolm's post above, that also gives us the Akashayana. <br /> <br /> That leaves only two Traditions: the Sahajiya, and the Solificati.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_